Third-party notices

This skill restates, in Cratis wording, ideas from morluto/rea (https://github.com/morluto/rea),
which is released under the MIT license: evidence rows that carry explicit unknowns, and the
executable-intake approach (static before dynamic, per-kind techniques, tracing a feature across
IPC, network and storage). No upstream text is reused.

This skill refers to material that `cratis-screenplay-legacy-extraction` adapts from agentic-engineer
and the Eventmodelers Build-Kits by Martin Dilger and Nebulit GmbH (https://nebulit.de), used with
the explicit consent of Martin Dilger and Nebulit GmbH. That material remains credited to them; see
the license file of that skill.
